tions"":""SAMEORIGIN"",""x-xss-protection"":""1; mode=block""}}",,"MADA Architectes — Architect in Casablanca
ArchitecteCasablanca3 yearsICE · 003881440000017
About
MADA Architects was founded by two young architects who believe that spaces should expand life, not complicate it. Inspired by the Arabic word “مدى” — Mada, meaning horizon, range, and possibility, the studio was born from a shared desire to design with clarity, intention, and human experience at the center. For us, architecture begins with understanding people — how they move, feel, breathe, and belong. Every line we draw is guided by a simple question: How can this space make life easier, calmer, and more meaningful? Our work blends the precision of architecture with the softness of lived experience. We design with light as a material, with the horizon as a guide, and with simplicity as a quiet act of respect. Whether shaping a home, a public place, or a small interior, we aim to create environments that feel effortless, grounded, and deeply connected to their context. At MADA Architects, we’re not driven by trends or noise. We’re driven by clarity. By purpose. By the belief that minimalism is not emptiness — it is room for life to grow. We build spaces that open possibilities. Spaces that breathe. Spaces that reach their own horizon. This is our Mada. Your Mada. The architecture of what’s possible.
